<title>UK: Former UK energy minister joins oil group - paper.</title>
<headline>Former UK energy minister joins oil group - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Former British energy minister Tim Eggar is to join the board of Monument Oil and Gas Plc in a move that could revive controversy over ex-ministers taking jobs in industries they have overseen, the Financial Times reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>Monument said the parliamentary watchdog on business appointments had given its approval, but the opposition Labour party accused Eggar of &quot;cashing in on expertise&quot; gained while a minister.</p>
<p>Eggar left the Department of Trade and Industry less than six months ago.</p>
<p>He plans to stand down as a member of parliament at the next election.</p>
</text>
